<%# locals: (id:, aria_label:, side: "right", classes: nil) %>
<%#
  Sheet component.

  Rendered via render_sheet (Gesso::Components::SheetHelper), which validates
  the side. This partial only renders markup.

  A side panel built on a native <dialog>, opened with the drawer
  Stimulus controller's showModal and dismissed by a backdrop click,
  Escape, or any close control inside it. Render it inside a
  [data-controller="drawer"] element alongside the trigger that opens
  it, and pass the panel contents as a block.

  This is the positioned dialog shell only — the panel header and body
  are supplied by the caller's block, so each sheet composes its own
  chrome.

  Params:
    id         - dialog id
    aria_label - accessible name for the dialog
    side       - "right" (default) or "left"
    classes    - extra CSS classes on the <dialog>
%>

<%= tag.dialog id: id,
      class: ["sheet", "sheet-#{side}", classes],
      aria: { label: aria_label },
      data: {
        drawer_target: "panel",
        action: "click->drawer#backdropClick"
      } do %>
  <%= yield %>
<% end %>
